#pragma once

// Copy to app/src/secrets.h and fill in. Gitignored (see the root .gitignore's `secrets.*`).
//
// flint's own net.cpp picks this up via `#if __has_include("secrets.h")` — app/src is already on
// the include path (`-Iapp/src` in platformio.ini), so this file stands in for flint's own
// include/secrets.h.example rather than needing a second copy of the same WiFi macros.
//
// OPENSEA_API_KEY is the piece flint's CLAUDE.md argues a unit should never carry: "No secrets on
// the device... if something seems to need a key, the design is wrong," naming Anchor as the reason
// for the rule. It is here anyway, as a deliberate, informed choice for this deployment — see the
// comment above FLINT_PROFILE_NETWORK in platformio.ini. Use a key scoped for this purpose, not the
// same one anchor-service runs with on the desktop: the two live in different trust domains, and a
// unit handed to someone at the offsite should not be able to spend anchor-service's own rate
// budget or need revoking through the same credential your desktop depends on.
#define WIFI_SSID "your-ssid"
#define WIFI_PASSWORD "your-password"
#define OPENSEA_API_KEY "your-scoped-read-only-key"
